# Copy to .env.local to enable optional features. The core app needs NONE of these.

# Enables the natural-language query box (/api/nl). Free tier is generous for
# this use case. Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Server-side only — never exposed to the browser.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...

# Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon token — enables cookieless page-view stats
# (visitors, referrers, countries, browsers). Optional; without it no analytics
# script is loaded at all.
#
# Get it from: Cloudflare dashboard → Analytics & Logs → Web Analytics →
# Add a site → copy the token out of the snippet it shows you.
#
# NOTE: the page is statically prerendered, so this is read at BUILD time.
# Set it, then run `npm run build`.
# CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN=abc123...

# Which Gemini model to try first, for both the plain-English box and the AI
# analysis. Optional: without it the built-in list in lib/geminiCall.ts is used,
# and that list is still the fallback when this one fails.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite

# The User-Agent sent to CDC WONDER. Optional: the default names this site
# ("MortalityDataPortal/1.0"). Set it to add a contact address CDC can reach,
# which is the courteous thing for an automated client to carry. It must not be
# left as Node's own "node": CDC's edge answers that with 403.
# WONDER_USER_AGENT=MortalityDataPortal/1.0 (+https://your-site.example/contact)
